        "body": "This PR adds a configurable SG Ready charger.\r\n\r\nRefs https://github.com/evcc-io/evcc/pull/7207, https://github.com/evcc-io/evcc/discussions/17731 and https://github.com/evcc-io/evcc/discussions/1875.\r\n\r\nThis really is just a custom charger with the Status/Enable/Enabled logic tweaked to treat Boost mode as enabled and Normal mode as disabled as suggested in https://github.com/evcc-io/evcc/pull/7207#issuecomment-2541806406:\r\n\r\n> Meiner Ansicht näch wäre es perfekt wenn der Charger bei PV Überschluss oder mit Ladeplan den SG-Ready Eingang 1 (Betriebszustand 3 \"forcierter Betrieb\") schalten würde. Dadurch würden die in der Wärmepumpe konfigurierten höheren Werte für WW und Heizen angefahren.\r\n\r\nConfiguration:\r\n\r\n```go\r\nSetMode   provider.Config\r\nGetMode   *provider.Config // optional\r\nPower     *provider.Config // optional\r\nEnergy    *provider.Config // optional\r\nTemp      *provider.Config // optional\r\nLimitTemp *provider.Config // optional\r\nMaxPower  *provider.Config // optional\r\nPhases    int // default 1, used to convert loadpoint current to max power\r\n```\r\n\r\nGet/Set Mode must handle the following modes (implementation follows what is done for battery control templates):\r\n\r\n1. Normal (SG Ready 0/0)\r\n1. Boost (SG Ready 1/0)\r\n1. Stop (SG Ready 0/1)\r\n\r\nTemp/ LimitTemp would most likely be used for reservoir or warm water temperature.\r\n\r\n**TODO**\r\n\r\n- [ ] handle `heating` group @naltatis \r\n- [ ] use stop mode together with SteuVE improvements (out of scope)",
