        "node_id": "I_kwDOLCdkCc6k0GYl",
        "number": 240,
        "title": "Questions about PNG decoding",
        "user": {
          "login": "center789",
          "id": 41336658,
          "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzM2NjU4",
          "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41336658?v=4",
          "gravatar_id": "",
          "url": "https://api.github.com/users/center789",
          "html_url": "https://github.com/center789",
          "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/center789/followers",
          "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/center789/following{/other_user}",
          "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/center789/gists{/gist_id}",
          "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/center789/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
          "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/center789/subscriptions",
          "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/center789/orgs",
          "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/center789/repos",
          "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/center789/events{/privacy}",
          "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/center789/received_events",
          "type": "User",
          "user_view_type": "public",
          "site_admin": false
        },
        "labels": [],
        "state": "open",
        "locked": false,
        "assignee": null,
        "assignees": [],
        "milestone": null,
        "comments": 0,
        "created_at": "2025-01-01T15:12:23Z",
        "updated_at": "2025-01-01T15:12:23Z",
        "closed_at": null,
        "author_association": "NONE",
        "active_lock_reason": null,
        "body": "\r\nWhen I tried to decode and display a PNG file, there were no errors, but the screen didn’t display it correctly. I thought it might be an issue with my PNG image, so I checked some related examples and used their PNG files as well, but they didn’t display either. Am I using the wrong method?\r\n```\r\nimport usys as sys\r\nsys.path.append('') \r\nimport machine \r\nimport lcd_bus\r\nimport lvgl as lv\r\nimport ili9488\r\n\r\nspi_bus = machine.SPI.Bus(\r\n    host=2,  \r\n    mosi=11,  \r\n    miso=-1,  \r\n    sck=12  \r\n)\r\n\r\ndisplay_bus = lcd_bus.SPIBus(\r\n    spi_bus=spi_bus,\r\n    dc=13,  \r\n    cs=10,  \r\n    freq=60000000  \r\n)\r\n\r\ndisplay = ili9488.ILI9488(\r\n    data_bus=display_bus,\r\n    display_width=320,\r\n    display_height=480,\r\n    reset_pin=9,\r\n    reset_state=ili9488.STATE_LOW,\r\n    backlight_pin=15,\r\n    backlight_on_state=ili9488.STATE_PWM,\r\n    color_space=lv.COLOR_FORMAT.RGB888,\r\n    color_byte_order=ili9488.BYTE_ORDER_RGB,\r\n    rgb565_byte_swap=False, \r\n)\r\n\r\n# display.set_color_inversion(True)\r\ndisplay.set_power(True)\r\ndisplay.init()\r\ndisplay.set_backlight(10)\r\ndisplay.set_rotation(1)\r\n\r\nlv.init()\r\nscr = lv.screen_active()\r\ntry:\r\n    script_path = __file__[:__file__.rfind('/')] if __file__.find('/') >= 0 else '.'\r\nexcept NameError: \r\n    script_path = ''\r\n    \r\nwith open('%s/png_decoder_test.png' % script_path, 'rb') as f:\r\n  png_data = f.read()\r\n#   print(png_data)\r\n\r\npng_image_dsc = lv.image_dsc_t({\r\n    'data_size': len(png_data),\r\n    'data': png_data \r\n})\r\n\r\nimage1 = lv.image(scr)\r\nimage1.set_src(png_image_dsc)\r\nimage1.set_pos(100,50)\r\n\r\n# Create an image from a symbol\r\n\r\nimage2 = lv.image(scr)\r\nimage2.set_src(lv.SYMBOL.OK + \" Accept\")\r\nimage2.set_pos(100,200)\r\n\r\n# Drag handler\r\n\r\ndef drag_event_handler(e):\r\n    self = e.get_target_obj()\r\n    indev = lv.indev_get_act()\r\n    vect = lv.point_t()\r\n    indev.get_vect(vect)\r\n    x = self.get_x() + vect.x\r\n    y = self.get_y() + vect.y\r\n    self.set_pos(x, y)\r\n\r\n# Register drag handler for images\r\n\r\nfor image in [image1, image2]:\r\n    image.add_flag(image.FLAG.CLICKABLE)\r\n    image.add_event_cb(drag_event_handler, lv.EVENT.PRESSING, None)\r\n```\r\n![2025](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/75bb2b24-5351-4fc1-8b87-775d08d9c25b)\r\n\r\nWhile checking if the PNG decoding feature was enabled, I noticed ```LV_USE_LIBPNG```. I looked it up and saw that it offers more advanced features, but enabling it (setting it to 1) causes a compilation error. Which one is recommended to enable?\r\n```\r\n/*LODEPNG decoder library*/\r\n#define LV_USE_LODEPNG 1\r\n\r\n/*PNG decoder(libpng) library*/\r\n#define LV_USE_LIBPNG 0\r\n```",
